1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:08,575
The fully loaded cost of an AI system on Akka is a fraction versus a hyperscaler or an assembled open-source stack.

2
00:00:08,575 --> 00:00:13,420
This is the combined cost across infrastructure, licenses, integration and people.

3
00:00:14,770 --> 00:00:18,105
We've seen many accounts report significant gains.

4
00:00:18,105 --> 00:00:28,350
Fox built a hyper-personalization system whose cores dropped from 150,000 to 22,000 after porting from Python to Akka.

5
00:00:28,350 --> 00:00:34,715
Verizon's infrastructure and cloud costs dropped by 70% due to our actor-based concurrency.

6
00:00:34,715 --> 00:00:44,115
At Manulife, they ported their LangChain agents to Akka and saw a 300% concurrency improvement and 99% drop in error rates.

7
00:00:44,115 --> 00:00:55,610
Swiggy improved multi-user concurrency watching their P99 latency drop from one hundred forty-four to seventy-one milliseconds at over five thousand predictions a second.

8
00:00:55,610 --> 00:01:03,695
Dojo was able to hire college graduates without any prior enterprise experience, and they delivered a regulated AI system in weeks.

9
00:01:03,695 --> 00:01:10,810
We helped a global, major bank port a decades-old payments system from mainframe to microservices in a few months.

10
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:13,875
How did Akka achieve these results?

11
00:01:15,225 --> 00:01:22,590
The hyperscalers charge for consumption: they measure every request, token and trace and then add it to your bill.

12
00:01:22,590 --> 00:01:25,855
Your cost grows with success and is hard to forecast.

13
00:01:25,855 --> 00:01:32,835
Akka charges a flat annual fee and extra use adds additional underlying hardware, but no additional Akka charges.

14
00:01:34,185 --> 00:01:39,600
Akka runs our stack on the lowest-priced hardware: compute, storage and network.

15
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:57,015
Your inference, AI controls, model routing, small language model training, agent execution, memory, workflows, messaging, governance, observability and evaluations all run on the same shared infrastructure.

16
00:01:57,015 --> 00:02:12,590
The hyperscalers, however, make their best margin on the managed AI services that they sell: agent runtime, memory, gateway, observability, evaluation and policy are designed to have extra overhead and cost more per request.

17
00:02:13,940 --> 00:02:22,020
Interpreted languages like Python carry a memory overhead for every session, and their concurrency models limit how many run on a node.

18
00:02:22,020 --> 00:02:31,850
Akka runs each session as a small actor, so a single Akka node holds millions of concurrent executions against a common shared compute.

19
00:02:31,850 --> 00:02:42,400
In Akka, sessions, agents, evaluations, guardrails, workflows, endpoints, data queries and timers all run as actors on the same node.

20
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:47,340
Akka's clustering spreads them across nodes and rebalances when a node leaves.

21
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:50,565
State is never lost, and sessions can continue uninterrupted.

22
00:02:51,915 --> 00:03:00,490
Assembled frameworks are allocated and managed separately, each keeping its own headroom that remains unused but something you still paid for.

23
00:03:00,490 --> 00:03:07,695
When you assemble multiple open source frameworks together, each makes a separate overhead allocation that compounds waste.

24
00:03:07,695 --> 00:03:18,065
In Akka, all of your services are running on the same shared compute model, and some customers run their nodes at nearly 95% utilization leading to significant efficiencies.

25
00:03:19,415 --> 00:03:28,125
Akka’s memory uses event-sourced entities: every change is recorded in a journal, and system of record data is accessible in memory.

26
00:03:28,125 --> 00:03:38,560
This creates the potential to recover any data from any point in time, and then read-write access to data is in low single-digit milliseconds without you needing to install a cache.

27
00:03:39,910 --> 00:03:48,365
Hyperscalers sell these functions as separate products, each its own layer, and you are responsible for integrating the different layers together.

28
00:03:48,365 --> 00:03:56,525
Akka ships the whole stack as one piece, already integrated, including orchestration, agent execution and memory.

29
00:03:56,525 --> 00:04:07,620
You do not need to acquire additional licenses for event streaming, caching, messaging, workflow orchestration, gateways, AI governance, observability, evaluations or red teaming.

30
00:04:08,970 --> 00:04:13,885
Akka works an optimization loop seeking for places to lower the cost of tokens.

31
00:04:13,885 --> 00:04:27,780
We search for avoidable costs: prompts that skip the cache, failed attempts, duplicate requests, reasoning above the median, unused tool definitions, or answers that run longer than needed.

32
00:04:27,780 --> 00:04:42,980
Akka then executes experiments around SLM training, self-hosting open weight models, making routing configuration changes, or giving feedback to end users in an effort to improve the balance of cost, performance and quality.

33
00:04:42,980 --> 00:04:46,755
Effective optimizations can lead to token reductions of up to 70%.

34
00:04:48,105 --> 00:04:52,195
Akka Specify runs a software factory for each of your projects.

35
00:04:52,195 --> 00:05:04,130
Your engineers, product managers, analysts and executives bring requirements as they already exist: hand drawings, spreadsheets, issue lists and broad descriptions.

36
00:05:04,130 --> 00:05:11,315
The factory writes the code, runs the system and checks it, and your people only make the decisions that need an understanding of your business.

37
00:05:11,315 --> 00:05:17,160
That means fewer handoffs between the business and engineering, and fewer people needed to get a system into production.

38
00:05:18,510 --> 00:05:29,365
Your organization sets its privacy, security, architecture and risk standards once, as exit conditions, and every factory checks them automatically.

39
00:05:29,365 --> 00:05:38,760
A system arrives at review having already passed the reviews you defined, so your reviewers read one complete record instead of running another cycle.

40
00:05:38,760 --> 00:05:48,815
When a system already exists, the original becomes the answer key, and every build is checked against it, so any drift fails the build months before acceptance testing.

41
00:05:48,815 --> 00:05:55,860
A global insurer rebuilt a 20-year-old underwriting calculator in under a week, matching the original case for case.

42
00:05:57,210 --> 00:06:08,310
Every system is designed from Akka components and documented by its factory, so an engineer who joins later reads what the system is for in its specification, not in the code.

43
00:06:08,310 --> 00:06:17,895
When a key engineer leaves, the knowledge stays with the system, and Specify keeps your existing systems current with best practice, so technical debt does not build up.

44
00:06:17,895 --> 00:06:25,910
Because each project runs its own factory, many run at once: we ported 65 open-source projects to Akka in parallel this way.

45
00:06:25,910 --> 00:06:31,055
The roadmap you planned for 2028 and 2029 can be delivered in 2027.

46
00:06:32,405 --> 00:06:43,910
A flat fee, the lowest-priced hardware, an efficient runtime, shared compute, an integrated stack, lower model spend and spec-driven development all add up.

47
00:06:43,910 --> 00:06:51,545
The fully loaded cost of an AI system on Akka is a fraction versus a hyperscaler or an assembled open-source stack.

48
00:06:51,545 --> 00:06:59,060
You do not need to acquire additional licenses to design, build, test, run or govern your AI systems.

49
00:07:00,410 --> 00:07:12,145
